# CVE Exception List for pip-audit (SPEC-082, RF-05)
# ===================================================
# Format: CVE-ID | Package | Reason | Decision Date | Review Date
#
# POLICY (SPEC-082, RFC-05):
# - Exceptions are NEVER automatic or global ("ignore all HIGH/CRITICAL")
# - Each exception requires: CVE ID, package name, justification, and decision date
# - Decision to add an exception is made by the LEAD, never the agent
# - Exceptions are auditable and tracked in version control
# - Each exception must include a review date (when it should be re-evaluated)
# - NO CONFIDENTIAL DATA in this file (only CVE IDs, package names, and generic reasons)
#
# HOW TO ADD AN EXCEPTION (requires LEAD approval):
#   1. Identify the CVE ID (e.g., PYSEC-2024-48 for black 23.12.1)
#   2. Verify it's in the pip-audit report: `pip-audit --desc --skip-editable`
#   3. Document package name, business justification, decision date, and review date
#   4. Uncomment/add the line below (following format exactly)
#   5. The CI workflow will parse this file and pass --ignore-vuln flags to pip-audit
#   6. Create a commit with message: "chore(security): exception CVE-XXXX (reason, review YYYY-MM-DD)"
#
# CURRENT EXCEPTIONS (approved by LEAD, 2026-10-02, as part of SPEC-082 pip-audit remediation):
PYSEC-2025-185 | python-jose | No fix_version published upstream (python-jose 3.3.0/3.4.0, CVE-2024-29370): JWE jwe.decrypt() DoS via crafted token with high-ratio compression (zip bomb pattern), excessive memory/CPU on decompress. Not exploitable here: this project's app/security/jwt.py uses ONLY jwt.encode/jwt.decode (JWS, signed HS256 tokens), never jose.jwe — the vulnerable decrypt() code path is never invoked in this codebase. | 2026-10-02 | 2026-12-02
PYSEC-2026-1325 | ecdsa | No fix_version, will never be fixed: upstream python-ecdsa maintainer declared side-channel attacks (Minerva timing attack on P-256, CVE-2024-23342) explicitly out of scope and recommends `cryptography` for timing-sensitive ops. Transitive dependency only (python-jose[cryptography]==3.4.0 requires ecdsa!=0.15), never imported directly by app code. Compensating control: app/security/jwt.py signs/verifies JWTs with HS256 (symmetric HMAC via `cryptography`/`pyca`), not ECDSA asymmetric signing — the vulnerable ecdsa.SigningKey.sign_digest() path is never exercised by this project's authentication flow. | 2026-10-02 | 2026-12-02
PYSEC-2026-1942 | starlette | Quadratic-time DoS via crafted HTTP Range header in FileResponse. Fix requires starlette>=0.49.1, which requires fastapi>=0.133.0, which requires pydantic>=2.7.0 (pydantic==2.5.3 pinned, out of scope for SPEC-082 — PLAN-011 only approved bumping 9 specific packages). DEFERRED, not dismissed as inapplicable: tracked as follow-up work requiring a dedicated pydantic 2.5.3->2.7+ migration SPEC (Lead decision, 2026-10-02). | 2026-10-02 | 2026-11-02
PYSEC-2026-161 | starlette | HTTP Host header not validated before reconstructing request.url (potential host-header-injection-adjacent issues downstream). Fix requires starlette>=1.0.1, blocked by the same fastapi/pydantic chain as PYSEC-2026-1942 above. DEFERRED pending pydantic bump (Lead decision, 2026-10-02). | 2026-10-02 | 2026-11-02
PYSEC-2026-2281 | starlette | StaticFiles on Windows vulnerable to SSRF via UNC path in os.path.realpath resolution. Fix requires starlette>=1.1.0, same fastapi/pydantic blocker. Risk reduced (this project deploys on Linux, self-hosted, ADR-005), but NOT excluded as inapplicable — deferred pending pydantic bump (Lead decision, 2026-10-02). | 2026-10-02 | 2026-11-02
PYSEC-2026-2280 | starlette | HTTPEndpoint selects handler by lowercasing HTTP method and attribute lookup, allowing dunder/attribute-access bypass in edge cases. Fix requires starlette>=1.1.0, same fastapi/pydantic blocker. DEFERRED pending pydantic bump (Lead decision, 2026-10-02). | 2026-10-02 | 2026-11-02
PYSEC-2026-249 | starlette | request.form() max_fields/max_part_size limits not enforced in affected versions (resource-consumption DoS via form parsing). Fix requires starlette>=1.3.1, same fastapi/pydantic blocker. DEFERRED pending pydantic bump (Lead decision, 2026-10-02). | 2026-10-02 | 2026-11-02
PYSEC-2026-248 | starlette | HTTP request path not validated before reconstructing request.url. Fix requires starlette>=1.3.0, same fastapi/pydantic blocker. DEFERRED pending pydantic bump (Lead decision, 2026-10-02). | 2026-10-02 | 2026-11-02
PYSEC-2026-2263 | pyasn1 | DoS via uncontrolled recursion when decoding ASN.1 data. Fix requires pyasn1>=0.6.3, but python-jose[cryptography]==3.4.0 declares pyasn1<0.5.0,>=0.4.1 (installing 0.6.3 breaks that declared constraint, confirmed via `pip check`). Verified: pyasn1 is used ONLY by jose/backends/rsa_backend.py and jose/backends/_asn1.py (RSA key ASN.1 encode/decode) inside python-jose; this project's app/security/jwt.py exclusively uses HS256 (symmetric HMAC, confirmed via grep — no RS256/ES256 anywhere in app/), so the RSA backend code path that invokes pyasn1 is never exercised at runtime by this codebase's actual JWT operations. | 2026-10-02 | 2026-12-02
